{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468370-wayward-and-weird-the-eldritch","id":1468370,"title":"[Wayward and Weird] The Eldritch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-19T15:02:42-08:00","id":1468370,"title":"[Wayward and Weird] The Eldritch","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Happy belated Halloween, I guess. I've been working on a homebrew Changeling project for some time now, a collection titled &quot;Wayward and Weird&quot; consisting of all sorts of strange ways the Lost can warp and weave into shapes unrecognizable sometimes even to themselves. Besides the Eldritch, below, I'll eventually be posting write-ups on changelings who find power in acting like villains, some perks for Loyalists, the odd thing that happens when you try to make a bargain directly with the Wyrd, and a few other tidbits. By the end I'll try to put it all together, maybe post it up on the ST Vault if I can ever actually figure out how to work layout software. This isn't a final draft, and comments and criticisms are always appreciated, or if you just want to call me a daft squimbo, that's fine too.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It\u2019s a tale as old as time: Power begets the desire for more power. The Satrap of Pearls, resplendent in all the glittering jewels of her bargaining acumen, one day finds she longs for the hobgoblin ties of the Baron of Lesser Ones and the reptilian wisdom of the Snake Librarian as well. It\u2019s not well known, especially among her let\u2019s say humbler peers, but there exists a means to be everything you\u2019ve ever wanted to be, and then some. It just takes a teeny, tiny sacrifice of what you once were.<br /> <br /> Autumn grimoires and Winter dossiers call them the Eldritch\u2014well, they call them many things, from true witch-queens to the face of the Lord\u2019s exiles to selfish bastards who\u2019ll doom us all, but \u201cEldritch\u201d is the most common epithet. The reasons for walking their path are myriad, but tend to boil down to, as mentioned above, a desire for ever more power, whether in order to better protect the freehold, put a definitive end to one\u2019s former Keeper, or a simple need for more of what you\u2019ve already got. Some Eldritch also see it as their duty to track down and squirrel away Titles that would be dangerous in the hands of their less enlightened siblings, whether because the oaths binding them are deceptively ruinous or because one has lain fallow for far too long to be safe or sane to wield.<br /> <br /> Most other Lost are wary of the Eldritch; they\u2019re strange, otherworldly, uncanny, frighteningly powerful, more than a smidge unpredictable, and prone to draw the attention of the True Fae. In fact, there\u2019s something a little Gentry-like about the way they act, changing roles and even identities like outfits. There\u2019s some resentment as well: Every new Title the Eldritch picks up for herself means one less blazon in the world for some poor common changeling with none at all. Why should the Scarecrow Minister also get to be the Magus of the Gilded Thorns <i>and </i>the Kraken Priest <i>and </i>the Shaman of the Moonlit Pines? You wanted to be the Shaman of the Moonlit Pines. That\u2019s just not fair. And so the Eldritch retreat to the edges and the moors, tending to their multifaceted concerns, holding court in their lavish Hollows for those who care to seek them out. More than one has ended up a Goblin Queen\u2014or more appropriately, Goblin Empress, staking claim to vast swathes of the Hedge, organizing legions of hob servants into factions devoted to each of her different Titles. You can imagine just how tense such a situation can get.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> To become one of the Eldritch, a changeling must have a Wyrd rating of six or higher. Having an Entitlement isn\u2019t required <i>per se</i>, but considering the primary benefit of Eldritchdom, most who chase this state already do. The changeling must then venture deep into the Thorns to find a Wyrd Altar (see below) at which to perform a sacrament of a paradigm shift requiring nine successes, sacrificing an Icon in the process\u2014the petitioner may unincorporate an already recovered Icon from her Clarity to do so if need be by spending a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings</b><ul><li>An Eldritch changeling can possess more than one Entitlement. The number of Entitlements she may hold at one time is equal to (Wyrd - 5). Each Title must be bequeathed or unearthed, and its accompanying Merit purchased, as normal. All of the Eldritch\u2019s heraldry tokens merge together into a coherent whole, although the changeling can only access the powers of her currently manifested Title\u2019s token.</li> <li>The changeling can still only embody one Entitlement at a time, but while doing so, her connections to other Entitlements and even her regular identity are obscured; rolls to gather information on the changeling or influence her life not based on her currently manifested Title suffer a penalty equal to (Wyrd - 5). This applies to fae attempts to track the changeling as well (at least until the pursuer gets wise to the Eldritch's current Entitlement).</li> <li>The changeling can change her currently manifested Title while in the Hedge with a subtle shift requiring one success.</li> <li>By touching the heraldry of an Entitlement and spending a point of Glamour, the Eldritch immediately learns all of the Title\u2019s salient details: Its name, the oaths attached to it, whether it\u2019s gone wild, etc. This power works on both claimed and unclaimed Titles.</li> <li>When swearing pledges, the changeling can choose to attach them to her Title. In doing so, she does not have to worry about breaking them while the Title is not manifested (although pledges based on time limits can still be broken if the changeling fails to fulfill her promise). A given Title may hold (Wyrd - 5) pledges at a single time.</li> <li>When becoming Eldritch, the changeling chooses a new name for herself, which for all supernatural purposes functions as her true name. While in the Eldritch state, her connection to her previous name is suppressed, meaning others cannot gain power over her from using it.</li> <li>When a character speaks the Eldritch\u2019s true name aloud three times in a row, the changeling immediately is made aware of this, as well as of the speaker\u2019s location. Reduce the total number of successes required to navigate the Hedge to reach the speaker in the same chapter by half, after applying all other modifiers.</li> <li>When successfully Hedgespinning or Dreamweaving in a way that resonates with her currently manifested Title, the Eldritch adds (Wyrd - 5) automatic successes to the roll. These successes must be allocated to the shift itself.</li> </ul><b>Curses</b><ul><li>When acting in a way that runs counter to the Eldritch's currently manifested Title (such as in the interests of a non-manifested one), the changeling suffers a Clarity attack using a dice pool of half Wyrd, rounded up.</li> <li>Those rare Eldritch who possess no Entitlement at all find their hearts pulled ever closer toward their claiming. A Titleless Eldritch who hears tell of or discovers a free Title must succeed on a Resolve + Composure roll or gain the Obsession Condition related to tracking the Title down and claiming it for her own.</li> <li>Any wild ranks of the changeling's Entitlements stack, affecting Clarity even while dormant. If the Eldritch's entire Clarity track is turned wild, additional wild ranks add one die each to Clarity damage rolls.</li> <li>If the Eldritch suffers the Cockaigne Condition for a particular Entitlement, changing to another Title instead requires a paradigm shift with three successes. Doing so suppresses Cockaigne so long as the changeling does not manifest its associated Title, but in its place she suffers from a different persistent Clarity Condition of the Storyteller\u2019s choosing. Even if she resolves this Condition, if she switches back to the wild Title, she gains the Cockaigne Condition once more, and can only resolve it by healing another point of Clarity damage.</li> <li>Perhaps most frightening of all, the Eldritch's status draws the notice of the Others, who begin to regard her as a potential rival to their Arcadian grandeur. Although this means one of the Gentry might be less likely to turn the Eldritch into a frog out of annoyance or whim, it also means constantly being watched by distant, hungry eyes that want you to come home, to your <i>true </i>home, and pledge your life to the mad game of immortals.</li> </ul><b>Leaving It All Behind</b><br /> <br /> Nothing has to last forever. For some Lost, the pressure of Eldritch status is too great to bear for too long. Others grow disgusted with what they\u2019ve become, too detached from their fellows, too much like the ones who stole her home away from her and plopped her down in this fairy tale nightmare to begin with. Some call it quits for more outr\u00e9 reasons: oaths sworn or broken, one final <i>fuck you</i> to a Huntsman that thinks it\u2019s got quite the fine little prize in its clutches, the pursuit of even greater arcane power by currying favor with the sinister things that cavort and slither through the cracks in reality. An Eldritch Lost can revoke her state by performing a paradigm shift requiring seven successes at a Wyrd Altar in the Thorns, ending with the sacrifice of her heraldry token, which splits and scatters to the four winds. The depowered changeling is saddled with her old name once more, and can never again take up any of the Entitlements she once possessed, even if she comes across them in the wild unclaimed.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <b>Wyrd Altars</b><br /> <br /> Even in the topsy-turvy dream-labyrinth of the Hedge, there are places more touched by the mystical than others. In the center of sun-dappled glades and the depths of mushroom-lit grottoes lie structures both material and conceptual known to the Lost as Wyrd Altars, singular temples to the maybe-sentient force of reciprocity and patterns that binds all fae beings together in a tricksy web. The majority of Wyrd Altars are found in the Thorns, stone slabs covered in twisting vines, the becalmed eye of an eternal maelstrom, the open grave at the back of the cemetery that just happens to have your very name carved onto the granite tombstone. They show up in other places too: other parts of the Hedge, Goblin Markets, dreams (often for just a single night), even in the real world, though changelings often find these last ones jealously guarded by mortal sorcerers who refer to them with some strange Greek name. There used to be exactly one in Arcadia; it's gone now. Even if they don\u2019t know what to call them or what exactly they can do, all fae can recognize Wyrd Altars on sight as places of imminent destiny. They are shrines where sacrifices can be made, bargains can be sealed, and all manner of otherwise unthinkable changes can be wrought on body, mind, and soul. The majority of known Wyrd Altars have a single transaction that can be made, often inscribed somewhere into the altar or carried on the songs of nearby passerines or in an urban legend all the teenagers in town tell around campfires to spook each other into amorous caresses. Those resting in the Thorns are generally broader in their scope, some able to carry out nearly any wish imaginable if only the petitioner has the courage and wit to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 11-21-2021, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T23:31:20-08:00","id":1468386,"title":"","content":"I can't tell for sure, but I'm under the impression the at least some of your math here will work better with (Wyrd - 4) instead of (Wyrd - 5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T15:07:24-08:00","id":1468430,"title":"","content":"I dont know what the Greek word is","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T21:05:19-08:00","id":1468459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468370-wayward-and-weird-the-eldritch?p=1468386#post1468386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't tell for sure, but I'm under the impression the at least some of your math here will work better with (Wyrd - 4) instead of (Wyrd - 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any particulars in mind? I stuck with (Wyrd - 5) for most calculations to keep the algebraic variable range between 1 and 5, though it's possible there are places I didn't think through all the implications. I did make a tweak to their Clarity attack rolls just now, though, after a little reflection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T03:16:59-08:00","id":1468479,"title":"","content":"The Clarity Attack was one, already a lot better, but there are two that I think are a problem:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468370-wayward-and-weird-the-eldritch#post1468370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>An Eldritch changeling can possess more than one Entitlement. The number of Entitlements she may hold at one time is equal to (Wyrd - 5). Each Title must be bequeathed or unearthed, and its accompanying Merit purchased, as normal. All of the Eldritch\u2019s heraldry tokens merge together into a coherent whole, although the changeling can only access the powers of her currently manifested Title\u2019s token.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>At Wyrd 6 this is 1. So you become an Eldritch for the purpose of holding more Titles and at first it means just one titles anyway, like everyone else. I think the Eldritch needs to have more access, so at least starting with 2 titles and going up to 6 would be nice. It can possibly be even more.<br /> <br /> This was the most glaring one and greatly influenced my first impression, but there is another:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468370-wayward-and-weird-the-eldritch#post1468370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>When swearing pledges, the changeling can choose to attach them to her Title. In doing so, she does not have to worry about breaking them while the Title is not manifested (although pledges based on time limits can still be broken if the changeling fails to fulfill her promise). A given Title may hold (Wyrd - 5) pledges at a single time.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Although it already gets better if the number of Titles is corrected, with just a few titles to begin with this seems rather weak, especially if people learn that the Eldritch can do that (which is likely to happen).<br /> <br /> It may be that tying multiple Pledges to a title isn't as good an idea, I'm not sure, but if this is the case I think getting rid of the calculation at all would be a better choice than leaving it as (Wyrd - 5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  fixing coding. 11-21-2021, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T18:25:11-08:00","id":1468718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468370-wayward-and-weird-the-eldritch?p=1468479#post1468479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Clarity Attack was one, already a lot better, but there are two that I think are a problem:<br /> <br /> <br /> At Wyrd 6 this is 1. So you become an Eldritch for the purpose of holding more Titles and at first it means just one titles anyway, like everyone else. I think the Eldritch needs to have more access, so at least starting with 2 titles and going up to 6 would be nice. It can possibly be even more.<br /> <br /> This was the most glaring one and greatly influenced my first impression, but there is another:<br /> <br /> <br /> Although it already gets better if the number of Titles is corrected, with just a few titles to begin with this seems rather weak, especially if people learn that the Eldritch can do that (which is likely to happen).<br /> <br /> It may be that tying multiple Pledges to a title isn't as good an idea, I'm not sure, but if this is the case I think getting rid of the calculation at all would be a better choice than leaving it as (Wyrd - 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>The pledge-compartmentalization I'm on the fence about. There was enough time passed between my first draft and this posting that I'm left wondering my rationale behind this. I'll probably efface it by the end, or at least sand away certain parts to redetail.<br /> <br /> Title count is intentional, as it mirrors the True Fae's own (inverse) progression. That's why I included the name-protection bits, so a Wyrd 6 Lost still gets something out of the whole shindig; it's not just lagniappe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}